        "source": "manual_review",
        "cve_id": null,
        "description": "Resembles arbitrary-file disclosure / path traversal: an authenticated endpoint fetches a Document by client-supplied pk and streams it back with a Content-Disposition filename, which scanners flag as IDOR/file-disclosure. It is actually safe: the object is loaded via get_object_or_404(Document, pk=pk) (ORM, parameterized) and gated by explicit ownership checks (patient users blocked unless doc.patient == request.user.patient_profile; clinicians blocked unless the patient is assigned or has an appointment with them). The served content is doc.file (a Django FileField, path managed by storage, not user input) and the filename is derived from doc.file.name.split('/')[-1] (basename only, no caller-controlled path component), so no traversal or unauthorized access is possible."
      },
      "false_positive_trap": true,
      "campaign_id": "v2-campaign-1",
      "provider_run": "kimi-code",
      "app": "healthcare-clinic-django"
