        "description": "Resembles missing authorization / IDOR on sensitive PHI: a VisitSummary is fetched by client-controlled pk via get_object_or_404 and rendered, which scanners flag as object-level access without checks. It is actually safe: the view applies role-aware ownership enforcement before rendering \u2014 patient callers get HttpResponseForbidden unless the summary is 'released' AND summary.patient == request.user.patient_profile, and clinician callers not owning the summary are routed through _patient_or_403, which denies access unless the provider is assigned to or has an appointment with the patient. The pk reaches only the parameterized ORM, so there is no injection and no unauthorized disclosure."
      },
